 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the QMC functionality as requested. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Files Modified:\n\n1. **include/qmc.hpp** - Added private members to the Sobol class and updated the interface\n2. **src/qmc.cpp** - Implemented all required functionality with C++20 and standard library only\n\n## Implementation Details:\n\n### Sobol Class\n- Implemented Sobol sequence generator in Gray-code order up to 32 dimensions\n- Dimension 1 uses van der Corput sequence, dimensions 2-32 use SOBOL_DATA\n- Point index 0 is the origin (all zeros)\n- next() returns coordinates in [0, 1) range\n\n### Brownian Bridge\n- Implemented Brownian bridge construction for n power-of-two time steps\n- Uses z[0] to fix W(T) and z[1] to fix midpoint, etc.\n- Proper variance calculation for each bridge step\n\n### Randomized QMC Asian Pricer\n- Implements arithmetic Asian call option pricing\n- Uses randomized quasi-Monte Carlo with digital shifts\n- Supports both Brownian bridge and forward construction methods\n- Returns both price estimate and standard error\n\n### Key Features:\n- **Accurate Normal Inverse**: Implemented with proper tail handling for safety\n- **Digital Shifts**: Randomized QMC using digital shifts for better convergence\n- **Memory Efficient**: Uses standard library only with no external dependencies\n- **C++20 Compliant**: Uses modern C++ features appropriately\n\nThe implementation has been compiled and tested successfully, showing correct Sobol point generation, Brownian bridge construction, and Asian option pricing functionality.",
